WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:09.758
In this video, we'll plan an overnight run,

2
00:00:09.758 --> 00:00:13.148
keep the laptop awake,
and check it in the morning.

3
00:00:13.148 --> 00:00:16.671
It's a real run, with the
night compressed: the agent

4
00:00:16.671 --> 00:00:19.861
sized the work to finish
in about eight minutes.

5
00:00:20.951 --> 00:00:25.419
In the chat with today's findings,
ask for a plan first: three new

6
00:00:25.419 --> 00:00:29.954
versions of our favorite, a demo
of each, and a draft pull request.

7
00:00:31.625 --> 00:00:35.586
The plan: three versions,
each tied to a finding.

8
00:00:35.586 --> 00:00:39.628
Draw Again, Portrait Dock,
and Labels + Shortcuts.

9
00:00:41.957 --> 00:00:45.615
Then test and record each one,
update the review page,

10
00:00:45.615 --> 00:00:49.139
open one draft pull request,
and keep a status file.

11
00:00:49.139 --> 00:00:50.968
It waits for your go-ahead.

12
00:00:54.061 --> 00:01:00.657
At bedtime, switch to Autopilot, so it
never stops to ask. Allow all stays on.

13
00:01:03.675 --> 00:01:05.731
Then: I'm going to sleep.

14
00:01:05.731 --> 00:01:10.173
Keep the laptop awake,
start the plan, run at most two

15
00:01:10.173 --> 00:01:14.614
sessions at once, and don't
merge or publish anything.

16
00:01:18.635 --> 00:01:22.075
It starts a helper that keeps
the laptop awake, writes the

17
00:01:22.075 --> 00:01:25.693
status file, and hands one
version to a background sub-agent.

18
00:01:25.751 --> 00:01:30.892
It checkpoints each version in Git as it
goes, and keeps the status file current.

19
00:01:31.816 --> 00:01:37.457
You can read the status file any time:
what's done, what's in progress, what's next.

20
00:01:37.457 --> 00:01:39.338
And what needs you: nothing.

21
00:01:43.243 --> 00:01:46.497
Overnight, it builds the
three versions, checks each

22
00:01:46.497 --> 00:01:50.003
one in the browser,
and records a narrated demo of each.

23
00:01:50.361 --> 00:01:55.324
A few of its own checks fail along the
way. It fixes them, and checks again.

24
00:01:56.743 --> 00:01:59.858
Then it opens one draft
pull request, and stops the

25
00:01:59.858 --> 00:02:02.851
keep-awake helper,
so the laptop can sleep again.

26
00:02:06.845 --> 00:02:11.800
Done. Three versions, three demos,
and nothing merged or published.

27
00:02:14.645 --> 00:02:18.143
In the morning, in the same chat:
what happened overnight?

28
00:02:21.812 --> 00:02:27.006
A summary, with links to the review page,
the morning report, and the pull request.

29
00:02:27.006 --> 00:02:30.824
It says what it checked,
and that nobody has tried these yet.

30
00:02:33.012 --> 00:02:36.399
Here's the Draw Again demo
it recorded, with captions.

31
00:02:37.512 --> 00:02:40.181
Each one is under half a minute, recorded in

32
00:02:40.181 --> 00:02:42.850
the background, with narration and captions.

33
00:02:45.264 --> 00:02:47.700
The review page links the pull request, too.

34
00:02:49.274 --> 00:02:55.455
And the draft pull request on GitHub,
stacked on the one from the synthesis.

35
00:02:55.455 --> 00:02:58.220
Nothing goes out until you say so.

36
00:02:59.074 --> 00:03:03.029
Next, we'll keep it running on another
computer, so you can close your laptop.
